<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal's BPI moves control of BFB unit.</title>
<headline>Portugal's BPI moves control of BFB unit.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco Portugues de Investimento said that its Banco de Fomento &amp; Exterior had bought the group's Banco Fonsecas &amp; Burnay (BFB) for 80 billion escudos.</p>
<p>BFE is controlled some 96 percent by BPI which had 100 percent of Banco Fonsecas.</p>
<p>BFE had already taken over another of the group's subsidiary banks, Banco Borges &amp; Irmao.</p>
<p>BPI said that the move was designed to strengthen the integration of its commercial bank operations.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon bureau 3511-3150035</p>
</text>
